 "name": "salmon_costume",
 "description": "Doug's homemade Chinook salmon costume (worn prop, anchor = Doug's hips, list after Doug at the same x/y/scale). Silver felt suit with a dark blue-green black-spotted back side, pink lateral stripe, white belly panel, zipper and scale ticks; spotted forked felt tail out of the lower back to about (-196,+110); small dorsal fin on the back; fin mitts on the suit sides. Blue-green hood forms a C round the back of the head, under the chin and over the cap dome, with a hooked silver 'kype' snout (eye, black gum line) jutting forward above the brim to (196,-262). Face and red cap stay clear. Bbox about x -196..196, y -352..110. Poses: float, wave, stand.",
